nativeps5 additions to AnyPS5 (AGC driver, pipeline pre-warm)
=============================================================

The nativeps5 work on this tree is licensed under the same terms as AnyPS5 (see LICENSE). The pipeline job pool, pipeline stamp,
draw fallback and pipeline-cache hardening (core/libs/prx/libSceAgcDriver/Graphics/{include,src}/PipelineJobs.*,
PipelineJournal.cpp, Pipeline.cpp, PipelineCache.cpp) were written with reference to the projects below. No source file of any of
them is included.

RPCS3 (GPL-2.0)
---------------
https://github.com/RPCS3/rpcs3 (read as a reference)

  - Draw with something compiled instead of skipping the draw while a pipeline builds (async shader mode with the interpreter as
    the stand-in: rpcs3/Emu/RSX/VK/VKGSRender.cpp get_graphics_pipeline / use_interpreter, VKShaderInterpreter.cpp), and the
    background compile pool at low priority (VKPipelineCompiler.cpp). The stand-in here is a compiled pipeline with the same shaders
    and render pass but different blend/depth/cull state, or a skipped draw that only writes render targets.
  - Placeholder entry in the pipeline cache before a compile starts so concurrent misses never compile twice
    (rpcs3/Emu/RSX/Program/ProgramStateCache.h).

RPCS3 ARM64 port "ARMSX3" (GPL-2.0)
-----------------------------------
https://github.com/ARMSX3 (read as a reference)

  - Persisting the Vulkan pipeline cache properly: temporary file plus rename, a header carrying the vendor/device/UUID of the
    driver, a size cap, validation at launch (vk/vkutils/device.cpp).

ARMSX2 (GPL-3.0): ideas only, no code
-------------------------------------
read for design only

  - A recorded pipeline-key list kept apart from the binary cache, replayed at start-up on a worker pool in three priority classes
    (Now / Ahead / Idle), where a waiting thread runs the job itself if no worker has started it, and where the key-list
    fingerprint leaves the driver version out so the list survives driver updates while the binary cache stamp includes it.
    PipelineJobs.cpp and PipelineJournal.cpp implement that design independently.
